{"id":"O","label":"SAME","label_reason":"Sub-question of the root: is the bottleneck statement-versus-English mismatch, and can a probe shrink the human audit of it.","scores":{"stakes":{"score":4,"reason":"Decides whether to build probe infrastructure or fund a full expert audit; either answer moves that build/collect choice."},"open":{"score":5,"reason":"Names models and labelled statements; measurements stop at nine models, 950 SMT-LIB encodings; Lean drift unmeasured within 250 H100-hours."},"internals":{"score":5,"reason":"Names an activation trace predicting correctness at 0.953 AUROC vs 0.674 for verbalized confidence, so outputs under-report internal doubt."},"reshape":{"score":5,"reason":"Four-step chain, probe fit in minutes leaves GPU idle; synthetic-transfer condition cheaply checkable; no source parallelises this chain here."}}}
{"id":"V1","label":"SAME","label_reason":"Same subject as the root's statement-matching sub-question, asking whether probes beat the judge ensembles pipelines already run.","scores":{"stakes":{"score":5,"reason":"Deploy decision turns on it: swap deployed judge ensembles for a cheaper probe or keep them, per-statement cost."},"open":{"score":5,"reason":"Same quantity and stopping point named; probe-versus-judge on natural Lean drift unmeasured and reachable within 250 H100-hours."},"internals":{"score":4,"reason":"Inherits the activation-trace claim but frames value as beating text-only judges; adds no new account of what outputs miss."},"reshape":{"score":3,"reason":"Names five-step chain and parallel labelling, but gives no checkable condition for computing the steps at once."}}}
{"id":"V2","label":"SAME","label_reason":"Still asks whether statement drift is detectable in a Lean formalizer's internals; adds a comparator and cross-model arm.","scores":{"stakes":{"score":4,"reason":"Chooses what to build: frozen probe on the formalizer or a fine-tuned contrastive evaluator; transfer results guide reuse."},"open":{"score":5,"reason":"Names models, labelled statements and a fine-tune per model; unknown above the 950-encoding scale, reachable with small open formalizers."},"internals":{"score":3,"reason":"Names hidden-state representations via a contrastive evaluator, but not what they add over the formalizer's outputs."},"reshape":{"score":3,"reason":"Five-step chain, but a fine-tune per model may already fill hardware, and no checkable parallelisation condition is named."}}}
{"id":"V3","label":"SAME","label_reason":"Sub-question of the root, narrowed to definition-level drift in research-level Lean formalization rather than a different subject.","scores":{"stakes":{"score":4,"reason":"Decides whether research-level definitions need a dedicated audit, and whether to invest in building the public corpus."},"open":{"score":4,"reason":"Open models measurable within reach, but the decisive Gemini reading is unmeasurable at any price, so key range lies beyond."},"internals":{"score":4,"reason":"Drift is an activation trace readable only with activation access; closed Gemini's outputs alone cannot show a definition drifted."},"reshape":{"score":3,"reason":"Four-step chain with GPU idle time, but synthetic perturbation is offered without a checkable transfer condition."}}}
